# Klingenberg Food — environment variables (technical plan §10d)
#
# NAMES ONLY. This file is committed; it must never contain a real value.
#
# THERE ARE NO SECRETS. The site is a static Next.js export with no server, no
# database and no third-party runtime service, so nothing here is a credential and
# nothing here is required. `npm run build` succeeds with no environment file at all,
# and the generated `out/` directory is served by any static host.
# `npm run check:policy` fails the build if a backend name reappears anywhere in the
# repository.
#
# One optional variable exists.

# --- Site ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The ONLY place a site domain may be configured. Everything absolute — canonical
# URLs, the sitemap, Open Graph, JSON-LD — resolves through lib/config/site.ts (§10d),
# and no other file may carry a domain literal.
#
# It states the FULL public address of the deployment, origin and sub-path both, and
# the sub-path is what next.config.ts builds its `basePath` from:
#
#   https://example.test           -> served at the root of a host, no base path
#   https://example.test/a-repo/   -> a GitHub Pages *project* site, base path /a-repo
#
# It is read at BUILD TIME and baked into the generated HTML, so the deployment that
# runs `next build` is what sets it — the GitHub Pages workflow takes it from
# `actions/configure-pages`, which reports the address GitHub assigned. Leave it empty
# locally: it falls back to http://localhost:3000 with no base path.
SITE_URL=
